{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NTEzMTIy","is_bot":false,"login":"tobias-tengler","name":"Tobias Tengler"},"baseRefOid":"9a563e814f3b6213c80a6bc96a01fbcb4d605096","body":"Fusion allocates a 13.6-million-entry reference table for each shared path-segment pool even when only the initial 4,096 slots are needed. Normal load retains about 104 MiB of slot storage.\n\nThis PR sizes the slot table to the current pool level and grows or shrinks it under the existing pool lock.\n\n### Benchmarks\n\nThe direct benchmarks construct and dispose the actual pool, or rent 6,145 arrays, return them, and trim twice. Pool levels match production; the microbenchmarks set the timer period to one day and invoke trim explicitly.\n\nBenchmarkDotNet 0.15.8, Release .NET 10.0.12 ARM64, server/concurrent GC: three launches, five warmup iterations and fifteen measured iterations per launch. Values are medians after BDN outlier filtering; ratios are relative to the baseline. Baseline `main` is `3a7d93b0ee`; the PR is `ceb7565bcf`.\n\nBoth variants use `DOTNET_GCDynamicAdaptationMode=0` for microbenchmarks and HTTP comparisons to avoid observed allocation-counter discontinuities. This is a measurement setting, not a production change; default-GC HTTP CPU/allocation effects are not independently established.\n\n| Case | Version | Median | Ratio | Allocated | Alloc Ratio |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Construct and dispose | `main` | 15.146 µs | 1.00 | 108,962,352 B | 1.00 |\n| Construct and dispose | PR | 2.208 µs | 0.15 | 33,040 B | 0.0003 |\n| Grow, return and trim | `main` | 82.125 µs | 1.00 | 573,720 B | 1.00 |\n| Grow, return and trim | PR | 82.058 µs | 1.00 | 778,616 B | 1.36 |\n\nConstruction uses one invocation per iteration, so its short timings are sensitive to timer and scheduling overhead. The forced growth/trim cycle allocates 204,896 B more (+35.7%), with overlapping timing ranges.\n\n### Verdict\n\nNormal-load heap captures show 108,929,312 B (103.9 MiB) less retained slot metadata, reproduced with default GC as well as fixed adaptation. No stable steady-state CPU or RSS improvement was established. Interleaved small-request CPU changes ranged from -0.03% to +8.56%. HTTP rates were capped by offered load, so these runs do not establish a throughput gain.\n\nRelease builds passed; 123 focused tests passed. [Full results and reproduction](https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/blob/ceb7565bcfd060fa85d94603c07661763ec486ef/PERFORMANCE-path-pool-slots.md).\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOBvrWZ88AAAABct1CBw","author":{"login":"github-actions"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"## Patch coverage\n\n**95.2%** of changed lines covered (20/21)\n\n| File | Covered | Changed | Patch % |\n|:-----|--------:|--------:|--------:|\n| […/Fusion/src/Fusion.Execution/Text/Json/PathSegmentPool.cs](https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/pull/10557/files#diff-af58e5e15459913a2c93bf7d23ecff6522a0977ac0be7921b463849fbabcbc3f) | 20 | 21 | 95.2%&nbsp;🟡 |\n\n<details><summary>Uncovered changed lines (JSON)</summary>\n\n```json\n{\n  \"sha\": \"ce1a8a5cca9ca056aa6355f0826a6ad8bd4da904\",\n  \"files\": [\n    { \"path\": \"src/HotChocolate/Fusion/src/Fusion.Execution/Text/Json/PathSegmentPool.cs\", \"ranges\": [[349, 349]] }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\nProject coverage: **59.0%** (311332/527641 lines)\n\n\n<!-- Sticky Pull Request Commentpatch-coverage -->","createdAt":"2026-10-16T18:26:29Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/pull/10557#issuecomment-6222070279","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"files":[{"path":"PERFORMANCE-path-pool-slots.md","additions":223,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/Directory.Build.props","additions":10,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/README.md","additions":72,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-perform